<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's QTC sees 1997 borrowing A$3.8 bln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's QTC sees 1997 borrowing A$3.8 bln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's Queensland Treasury Corporation (QTC) said its indicative gross borrowing requirement for calendar 1997 is A$3.785 billion.</p>
<p>This compared with actual raisings in 1996 of A$4.793 billion, against an estimate of A$3.569 billion, QTC said.</p>
<p>&quot;The variance largely reflected the temporary floating rate funding arrangements associated with the formation of Metway Bank (includes Suncorp and QIDC),&quot; QTC said in a statement.</p>
<p>QTC is the borrowing arm of the state of Queensland.  </p>
<p>QTC said its borrowing requirements would be reviewed at June 30, 1997, and an estimate for the 1997/98 financial year to June 30 would be made at that time.</p>
